WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.725
BRETT MORGAN: With almost
500 sessions at Next 2019,

00:00:02.725 --> 00:00:05.100
it's understandable that you
couldn't get to all of them.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.770
So if you didn't get to see
Build Mobile Apps with Flutter

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.860
and Google Maps, then stay
tuned because here's the rewind.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.250
As a developer
relations engineer,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.870
I often hear from
developers that they

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.360
need to develop mobile
experience for their customers

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.530
faster, and they want their
app to be a joy to use.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.870
Flutter allows developers
to write once and deploy

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.730
everywhere, saving time
and money by developing

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.890
for both Android and iOS using
one development team and one

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.380
code base.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.200
Developers usually love coding
with Flutter as we empower them

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.150
with stateful hot
reload, which gets

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.540
their changes onto their
device just by hitting Save

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.040
in their editors, which is
exactly what our talk at Cloud

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.540
Next was all about.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.250
Here is a quick
montage of the app

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.830
I built live on stage
in San Francisco,

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.470
mapping out the ice cream stores
around the conference center.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.720
We started, as always,
with hello world.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.790
Then we connect
Google Cloud Firestore

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.860
to get a list of
ice cream stores.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.490
Next, we exposed a list of these
stores using List View Builder

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:04.680
and added Google Map to
enable us to visualize

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.540
where the stores are.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.910
We then utilized Google
Maps web services

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.290
to retrieve photos
for the stores.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:13.770
And as one final flourish,
we built a carousel

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:17.280
to enable users to swipe through
the list of stores easily.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.860
To watch the full talk, check
out the link in the description

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:20.597
below.

00:01:20.597 --> 00:01:22.680
And don't forget to subscribe
to the Cloud YouTube

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.840
channel for more great
Next Rewind content.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:26.700
Thanks for watching.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.050
[MUSIC PLAYING]

